{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:11WorldModule0A8SnapshotV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WorldSnapshot"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"WorldSnapshot"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Snapshot.swift#L33","fileName":"Snapshot.swift"},"title":"WorldSnapshot","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WorldSnapshot"},{"kind":"text","text":"<each "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" repeat each "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Se","text":"Decodable"},{"kind":"text","text":", repeat each "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SE","text":"Encodable"},{"kind":"text","text":", repeat each "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Component","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule9ComponentP","text":"Component"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/SavingAndLoadingWorlds"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use a snapshot to save a world and restore it later, or to compare two worlds. A snapshot"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":", so you can encode it with any encoder, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"JSONEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":". Take one with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/snapshot(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", listing the component types to save, and rebuild a world from it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"World(restoring:)"},{"type":"text","text":". Each component type you save must conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example saves a world as JSON and restores it:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Foundation","","var world = World()","let ship = world.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 2), Health(current: 3))","let data = try JSONEncoder().encode(world.snapshot(Position.self, Health.self))","","let decoded = try JSONDecoder().decode(WorldSnapshot<Position, Health>.self, from: data)","let restored = World(restoring: decoded)","print(restored[Position.self, of: ship])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every entity handle, live or stale, means the same in the restored world as in the original,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so handles you saved elsewhere stay valid. The restored world also hands out the same handles","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from later spawns.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A snapshot holds no resources, hooks or change ticks, and the restored world’s components"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are all added at its first tick. To save resources too, or to save a world without listing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its types at each call, use a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Scene","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decoding throws "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DecodingError.dataCorrupted"},{"type":"text","text":" for data that no world could have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produced, such as a component of an entity that isn’t live."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note"}]}],"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/Se","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/SE","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/WorldSnapshot\/init(from:)"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/WorldSnapshot\/count"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/WorldSnapshot\/encode(to:)"]},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/WorldSnapshot\/Equatable-Implementations"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/worldsnapshot"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A saved copy of a world’s entities, hierarchy and the components of the listed types."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Saving-and-Loading-Worlds","title":"Saving and Loading Worlds","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/SavingAndLoadingWorlds","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documenta